(1277037, 162403, 35804, '<td valign="top">Ok...I''m sure you have a million comments about this scene, there is a place for something like this and I''m not sure it is here. It reminds me of something somebody "young" would do, refering to setting something like this up and photographing it, and all the while thinking they are being shocking, bold, etc....I''ve spent some long years in "art" school and saw alot of things like this, things that make this look like Sesame Street, perhaps I''m jaded, perhaps todays society needs things to be blatant and unkind, but this is what I learned...there is nothing shocking or new, and eventually we grow out of thinking what we are doing is.</td>', 'Ok...I''m sure you have a million comments about this scene, there is a place for something like this and I''m not sure it is here. It reminds me of something somebody "young" would do, refering to setting something like this up and photographing it, and all the while thinking they are being shocking, bold, etc....I''ve spent some long years in "art" school and saw alot of things like this, things that make this look like Sesame Street, perhaps I''m jaded, perhaps todays society needs things to be blatant and unkind, but this is what I learned...there is nothing shocking or new, and eventually we grow out of thinking what we are doing is.', '2005-04-07 10:51:47.000000', NULL, 1),
