(1288366, 163461, 26505, '<td valign="top">I knew you were bound for greatness! Congrats!!!!</td>', 'I knew you were bound for greatness! Congrats!!!!', '2005-04-13 11:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1288376, 163426, 35044, '<td valign="top">I like the abstract composition of this shot.  The "Y" is obvious and it meets the criteria.  Good creativity.  The cropping is good: I like the compositional movement from the bottom left corner and the use of negative space.  <br/> <br/>The nature of the shot is relatively abstract - any detail will be limited.  It also means that any distraction in the shot will be a big distraction, with so little else to look at.  The right hand fork is either a slight double exposure or is hair resplitting - it detracts from the purity of the image, as does the blip halfway down the same fork.  The left hand fork appears fractionally out of the shallow DoF, leaving a slight blur.  There is a very slight shadow on the bottom LHS.  None of these points would matter, but for the focus that is forced into the detail by the degree of abstraction utilised.<br/> <br/>Overall, I like this image, but in the competition I skipped over it too quickly when voting.  I gave you a 4, but on reflection, the skill in getting the photo and the creativity and composition should have led me to vote higher - 5 or 6 (and I tend to give very few high marks, I have noticed).<br/> <br/>The image was not attention grabbing enough, IMO, to score highly.  It was sufficiently similar in shape to a number of "stick" photos so that it did not stand out.  It is an attractive image.  Your score does not reflect the quality of the image, merely the voting patterns in these particular circumstances!</td>', 'I like the abstract composition of this shot.  The "Y" is obvious and it meets the criteria.  Good creativity.  The cropping is good: I like the compositional movement from the bottom left corner and the use of negative space.   The nature of the shot is relatively abstract - any detail will be limited.  It also means that any distraction in the shot will be a big distraction, with so little else to look at.  The right hand fork is either a slight double exposure or is hair resplitting - it detracts from the purity of the image, as does the blip halfway down the same fork.  The left hand fork appears fractionally out of the shallow DoF, leaving a slight blur.  There is a very slight shadow on the bottom LHS.  None of these points would matter, but for the focus that is forced into the detail by the degree of abstraction utilised. Overall, I like this image, but in the competition I skipped over it too quickly when voting.  I gave you a 4, but on reflection, the skill in getting the photo and the creativity and composition should have led me to vote higher - 5 or 6 (and I tend to give very few high marks, I have noticed). The image was not attention grabbing enough, IMO, to score highly.  It was sufficiently similar in shape to a number of "stick" photos so that it did not stand out.  It is an attractive image.  Your score does not reflect the quality of the image, merely the voting patterns in these particular circumstances!', '2005-04-13 11:19:33.000000', NULL, 0),
