(1292321, 163677, 27735, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fredisdead:</b></div><hr/><i> beautiful - like so many have said before me. very very graphic, stark and striking colour balance.  i love the totally flat textureless sky - does just right for the composition (any brushing? please say "no"!). bye, fred. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nope, no "brushing". I added my post processing steps to the photo description.</td>', 'Originally posted by fredisdead: beautiful - like so many have said before me. very very graphic, stark and striking colour balance.  i love the totally flat textureless sky - does just right for the composition (any brushing? please say "no"!). bye, fred.   Nope, no "brushing". I added my post processing steps to the photo description.', '2005-04-14 17:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1292394, 162518, 14763, '<td valign="top">Thank for all the comment.  As for Shooting Snow Shots First may sure that the sun in not shining on the snow don''t shoot  into the sun.  What works best for me is to shoot with the sun to my back.  <br/> <br/>As for Editing I started with this <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=166499" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14763/thumb/166499.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14763/thumb/166499.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14763/thumb/166499.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Then adjusted levels which gave me this<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=166500" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14763/thumb/166500.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14763/thumb/166500.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14763/thumb/166500.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Then Unsharp Mask With Treshold 0 Amount 3 Radius 2<br/>Neat Image <br/>Unsharp Mask again with the same settings <br/>Adjusted Bright &amp; Constrast  <br/>Which give me the final photo<br/> <br/>Thanks so much I hope this will help you in the future.</td>', 'Thank for all the comment.  As for Shooting Snow Shots First may sure that the sun in not shining on the snow don''t shoot  into the sun.  What works best for me is to shoot with the sun to my back.   As for Editing I started with this    Then adjusted levels which gave me this   Then Unsharp Mask With Treshold 0 Amount 3 Radius 2Neat Image Unsharp Mask again with the same settings Adjusted Bright & Constrast  Which give me the final photo Thanks so much I hope this will help you in the future.', '2005-04-14 18:13:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1292435, 163540, 35239, '<td valign="top">Wow, I didn''t see that shot when I voted, boo<br/> :(<br/>I think it''s a great shot, and again I am dissapointed at the people who probably voted low on this because they can''t stand to see nudity or near nudity.<br/> <br/>If it wasn''t for that, I am pretty sure you would have made it to the top, or at least the top 3.<br/> <br/>Congrats on a great shot (and the model for a great cleavage!)</td>', 'Wow, I didn''t see that shot when I voted, boo :(I think it''s a great shot, and again I am dissapointed at the people who probably voted low on this because they can''t stand to see nudity or near nudity. If it wasn''t for that, I am pretty sure you would have made it to the top, or at least the top 3. Congrats on a great shot (and the model for a great cleavage!)', '2005-04-14 18:41:46.000000', NULL, 0),
