(1292665, 162398, 35229, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vasc:</b></div><hr/><i> you should''ve preserved the blue in the sky instead of turning it cyan, however it''s a very good photo (maybe less dodging in the sky?) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I am not sure what you mean, I did not turn anything cyan, and no dodging did occur. Maybe your monitor is playing tricks?</td>', 'Originally posted by vasc: you should''ve preserved the blue in the sky instead of turning it cyan, however it''s a very good photo (maybe less dodging in the sky?)  I am not sure what you mean, I did not turn anything cyan, and no dodging did occur. Maybe your monitor is playing tricks?', '2005-04-14 20:43:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1292667, 162398, 35229, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kpriest:</b></div><hr/><i> Wait! I know this one... "N x M =" - "Power to the People!"<br/>Am I right? What do I win?<br/>Nice shot - maybe a tighter crop on top and bottom. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes you could be right there but it looks like it equals 6.029<br/>.</td>', 'Originally posted by kpriest: Wait! I know this one... "N x M =" - "Power to the People!"Am I right? What do I win?Nice shot - maybe a tighter crop on top and bottom.  Yes you could be right there but it looks like it equals 6.029.', '2005-04-14 20:44:25.000000', NULL, 0),
